## Distinct problems

<SplitTable ticket={4471} />

## Why subject deduplication failed

The earlier triage decision merged reports when their subject lines matched. For date bugs,
reporters wrote similar subjects for completely different failure modes:

- The shared date parser reading month-first in European locales where day is written first.
- The `booking-v3` form printing an `MM/DD/YYYY` format hint while parsing `DD/MM/YYYY`.
- Timezone conversion shifts moving meetings across midnight boundaries by one day.
- Clock skew / race conditions causing invite delivery timestamps to precede booking creation.

Splitting #4471 into dedicated issues ensures engineering fixes each root cause independently.

